## Email confirmation links are dead — ConfirmEmail/ConfirmEmailChange pages missing

### Status
Fixed.

### GitHub Issue
#105

### Summary
`/Account/ConfirmEmail` and `/Account/ConfirmEmailChange` were never scaffolded. With
`RequireConfirmedAccount = true` (set by #94), new local accounts can never confirm and
can never sign in; email-change confirmation links are equally dead.

### Reported Behavior
Found during an account-management audit, not user-reported. No code calls
`UserManager.ConfirmEmailAsync`/`ConfirmEmailChangeAsync`, and no such page exists under
`Areas/Identity/Pages/Account/`.

### Expected Behavior
Following a registration or email-change confirmation link actually confirms the account
or applies the new email.

### Root Cause
- `Services/EmailConfirmationLinkSender.cs:54-59` builds a callback to
  `page: "/Account/ConfirmEmail"` (used by Register, ResendEmailConfirmation,
  ExternalLogin, and `Manage/Email.cshtml.cs`'s `OnPostSendVerificationEmailAsync`).
- `Manage/Email.cshtml.cs:153-157` (`OnPostChangeEmailAsync`) builds a callback to
  `"/Account/ConfirmEmailChange"`.
- Neither page was scaffolded when #94 wired up email verification, and no handler calls
  the corresponding `UserManager` confirm methods.
- Uncaught because `EmailModelTests.cs` never exercises the email-sending branch, and
  `RegisterTests.cs` never follows the actual emailed link.

### Proposed Fix
1. Scaffold `Areas/Identity/Pages/Account/ConfirmEmail.cshtml(.cs)` — decode `code`, call
   `ConfirmEmailAsync`, show success/failure.
2. Scaffold `ConfirmEmailChange.cshtml(.cs)` similarly — `ChangeEmailAsync` +
   `RefreshSignInAsync`.
3. Keep both in the generator's default style, per CODING_CONVENTIONS.md.
4. Update `Spec/Features/FEATURES-email-verification.ospec`'s Status to match reality.
5. Add tests following the real confirm links (registration confirm, email-change confirm,
   and an invalid/tampered-token failure case) rather than stopping at token generation.

### Acceptance Criteria
- Following a registration confirmation link confirms the account and allows sign-in.
- Following an email-change confirmation link applies the new email.
- An invalid/expired token fails gracefully, not with an unhandled exception.
- `FEATURES-email-verification.ospec` Status reflects reality.
- Tests cover the actual confirm-link flow for both cases.

### Out of Scope
- `DeletePersonalData.cshtml.cs` cascade/orphan behavior — separate discussion.
